.TH BACAK-SESSION-LAUNCHER 8 "June 2026" "BDM 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bacak-session-launcher \- final stage of a BDM login; execs the desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacak-session-launcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bacak-session-launcher
is the last stage of a Bacak Display Manager login. By the time it runs,
.BR bacak-display-manager (8)
has already dropped privileges to the target user and exported the base
environment. The launcher therefore runs wholly unprivileged.
.PP
It reads the chosen session's command and identifier from the environment,
wraps the session in a D-Bus user session when needed, and
.BR execve (2)s
the session so it becomes the process the daemon waits on. Isolating this
varied, third-party-heavy step in a tiny unprivileged binary keeps the
privileged daemon small and auditable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BDM_SESSION_EXEC
The session command (from the
.I Exec=
line of the session's desktop entry).
.TP
.B BDM_SESSION_ID
The session identifier (desktop-entry basename).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bacak-display-manager (8),
.BR bacak-greeter (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Bacak Desktop Project.
